Coding agents write and push faster than most CI systems were designed to
serve. The open problem is verification: how do you keep a fail-closed merge
gate when the suite already ran on a laptop or agent machine, and when the
cloud re-run is either too expensive, too slow, or both?

**thwip** is our answer so far, now in public beta. It is a control plane and a
small protocol for *commit-carried CI evidence*: you run approved checks where
the code lives, sign a compact proof of the exact Git tree, and a
ruleset-protected GitHub App verifies that proof before merge. We treat this
as research in verifiable agent coding, with a working product attached so the
claims stay falsifiable.

